From 3fec3834f05112889857e5f78dc39bc92b7aa502 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 20:26:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix projector, ink, timer and discussion wiring

Site-code only. No Notion lesson content, states or structure touched.

Assigned tools never embedded
- liveAssignedToolRoute now drops a trailing dash qualifier and falls back to
  longest-key prefix match. "Distributive Area Method" and its "- teacher
  display" / "- equation phase" / "- optional support" variants all resolved
  to null against the distributivearea key, so every Area Tool step in
  M1.T1.L1-D1 failed to embed on any surface, silently.

Blank projector on direct instruction and guided practice
- Board mode follows boardOpen instead of a hardcoded i-do/we-do/manip list.
  Those states were handing the projector an unwritten ink canvas and
  discarding Main Display, so the authored mathematics never reached the room.
- The board renders mainDisplay || body, keeping the mathematics behind the ink.

Ink surfaces were on different channels
- present's two InkBoard mounts used session.id while /ipad and /board
  broadcast on ink-main. The projector board could never receive a stroke.
- ScreenInkOverlay is now mounted on /teacher/pace; write-on-screen existed
  only on /present, so the support projector could not be annotated.

Hustle and Settle erased themselves
- Control's snapshot is a full replace and omitted interlude and transition,
  so republishing (about once a second while a timer runs) deleted the
  interlude, and auto-advance then skipped the transition. Both fields are
  carried through, and auto-advance is gated on an active interlude.
- Same class of bug: remoteActions and slideOverlay were absent from
  sequence.steps but read back on rehydrate, so any reconnect wiped the iPad's
  Remote Actions and every slide overlay.

Discussion
- Back on round 1 now steps out to the previous lesson state instead of
  sitting disabled. The overlay covers Control at z-index 50, so Control's own
  Back was unreachable and Close was the only exit.
- The discussion branch outranks a resolved lesson visual, which was silently
  dropping the stems and vocabulary aside.

Escalating countdown warning (Steele's ask)
- New src/lib/timerUrgency.ts: amber at 30s, coral and pulsing at 15s, faster
  at 5s. Applied to the main projector, the pace screen and the student device
  so a head-down student gets the same runway the room gets. The student
  threshold moved from 10s, which was too late to be a warning at all.
  Colour and opacity only, never layout; colour survives reduced-motion.

Also: AREA_MODEL_SKIP_STATES is checked against the raw class-state id as well
as the stage id, so the warmup and learning-check skips actually fire.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
